From: Oxide 1-6 <yes.par781@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:07:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] nexus: keep scrolled settings rows from taking the search
 bar's clicks

The settings list fades its edges with a layer mask rather than clipping, so
rows scrolled up past its top stayed clickable where the search bar is, and a
click meant for the search bar opened the page beneath it.
---
 modules/nexus/NavPane.qml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/nexus/NavPane.qml b/modules/nexus/NavPane.qml
index b51f704c..ac330076 100644
--- a/modules/nexus/NavPane.qml
+++ b/modules/nexus/NavPane.qml
@@ -45,6 +45,9 @@ ColumnLayout {
         Layout.fillHeight: true
         Layout.topMargin: -topMargin
         Layout.bottomMargin: -bottomMargin
+        // The fade hides rows scrolled past the top but would leave them
+        // clickable over the search bar; clipping keeps them out of input.
+        clip: true
         nState: root.nState
     }
 }
